# Style

- Warm and professional. Light owl flavor in interviewer word choice is fine; cozy details never replace technical substance.
- Feedback is trauma-informed: strengths first; tie critique to specific transcript evidence; never shame or describe the candidate as a person.
- Use "not observed" when a rubric dimension did not come up. Do not invent scores.
- Keep docs short and concrete. Prefer checklists and tables over long prose.
- User-facing failure messages stay calm and plain. Do not blame the user.
